== VERDICT T-7 / X-2: the --max-time 5 arm IS reached. This is its first live measurement. ==
  1. EXACTLY 1 'topology poll got no answer' line (edge-triggered), at 00:34:57.065.
  2. The line reports 'after 12.033s (each request bounded at 2s connect / 5s total)'.
  3. curl's own diagnosis in the kernel log, repeatedly:
       curl: (28) Operation timed out after 5002 milliseconds with 0 bytes received
     THAT is the discriminator. 08-31's iptables SYN-drop produced
       'Failed to connect ... after 2001 ms'  (the --connect-timeout arm).
     5002 ms per request = the --max-time 5 bound firing. X-2 is answered on its own terms.

  CAVEAT I am NOT rounding away: the rider PREDICTED ~15 s (3x5 s); the measurement is
  12.033 s. That is neither ~6 s (the already-known connect arm) nor the predicted 15 s.
  I did not attribute the ~3 s difference. A plausible but UNTESTED explanation is that the
  poll straddled the transition -- Ryu was killed at ~00:34:4x and the stall listener bound
  at ~00:34:5x, so at least one of the three requests may have met a closed port rather than
  the stall. Recorded as an open detail, not explained away.

  4. The 'exactly 1 line' result has discriminative power here, because the poll thread is
     provably still alive afterwards: 48 kernel threads, the kernel still answers
     /ndt/get_graph_data 200, and 'Command failed (exit code 28): curl ... /stats/flow/2'
     lines keep appearing after the WARN. So the single line is edge-triggering, not a
     thread that died on the first round.

  5. MY OWN INSTRUMENT ERROR, corrected: the step-5 witness reported 0 curl children because
     it filtered on ppid == kernel pid. curl is a GRANDchild -- the kernel forks sh, sh forks
     curl (observed live: pid 1202341 'sh' with ppid 1009541, pid 1202342 'curl' with ppid
     1202341). The per-child ~15 s lifetime therefore was NOT measured; the timing evidence
     above rests on the kernel's own 'after 12.033s' and on curl's 5002 ms diagnosis.

  6. SIDE EFFECT that turned out to be the round's best result: stopping Ryu made all ten
